.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Generated art was ignored while the site ran on the machine that drew it: the
# pictures were already sitting next to the server, and they are regenerable, so
# the history was not worth the size.
#
# The site now runs on a host with no graphics card. The pictures are drawn at
# home and there is no other way for them to reach the server, so they travel
# the way everything else does. Roughly 50MB, growing by a few hundred KB per
# picture that somebody keeps.
# assets/

# Thumbnails, though, stay out. Those genuinely are rebuilt on demand, and there
# are several per picture. Both trees, because pictures attached to a page are
# thumbnailed exactly like generated art is, and repo-sync commits files/.
assets/**/.thumbs/
files/**/.thumbs/

# content/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the campaign itself, it is only
# ~100KB, and it is the one thing here that cannot be regenerated. Five people
# can write to it through the MCP server, so its history is the undo button.

# How this machine starts the dev server. Points at whatever interpreter the
# person running it happens to have, so it is local by definition. Anything
# genuinely shared under .claude/ can still be committed.
.claude/launch.json

# Set by repo-sync when a pull brings code the running process does not have
# yet, cleared once that code is serving. Purely local state about one machine.
.needs-restart

# Shared secret for the MCP server. Never commit this.
.mcp-token

# Generated Obsidian vault. Rebuild with tools/export_obsidian.py.
vault/

# Generated static site. Rebuild with tools/export_site.py.
site/

# Shared password for the wiki. Never commit this.
.wiki-password

# Per-person MCP tokens. Never commit these.
.people-tokens.json

# Wiki accounts and session key. Never commit these.
.accounts.json

# Wiki accounts and session key. Never commit these.
.session-secret

# SRD reference data. Regenerate with tools/fetch_srd.py.
data/srd.json

# Which Discord messages have been dealt with. Local state, like a cursor.
.inbox.json

# Uploaded attachments. NOT ignored: a scanned map or a handout cannot be
# regenerated from anything, unlike assets/.
# files/

# The shared passphrase, stored as a scrypt hash. Never commit it.
.wiki-passphrase


# Which process is serving. Written at startup, meaningless elsewhere.
.server-pid

# Marks a machine with no graphics card, so the art panel queues requests
# rather than offering a button that cannot work. Per-machine by definition:
# the server has one of these and the machine at home must never get it.
.no-gpu

# Breadcrumbs from the windowless art drain. Local, and rotated.
.draw-queued.log
